h rotated and cropped images achieved 63.73% IoU. However, it largely increases the training time. Using the transfer learning VGG, we achieve 73.74% average pixel accuracy and 58.45% average IoU on the test set. In addition, we achieve 78.03% average test pixel accuracy and 64.04% average test IoU by the method of U-Net. Finally, we build a new model named Mobile-Deeplabv3+, and we achieved 83.56% average pixel accuracy and 71.35% average IoU on the test set.","topics":[],"score":287933,"global_rank":28747,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":6098},{"name":"FredHutch/nextflow-aws-batch-squared","owner":"FredHutch","html_url":"https://github.com/FredHutch/nextflow-aws-batch-squared","stars":10,"forks":3,"watchers":8,"issues":4,"language":"Python","description":"Run Nextflow on AWS Batch (Squared)","topics":[],"score":287910,"global_rank":28759,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":6099},{"name":"vlandeiro/yamlett","owner":"vlandeiro","html_url":"https://github.com/vlandeiro/yamlett","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Yet Another ML Experiment Tracking Tool","topics":[],"score":287902,"global_rank":28763,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":6100}]